{"nodes": [{"id": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence", "label": "ADR-0004 Hybrid persistence: in-memory and PostgreSQL", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_hybrid_storage", "label": "Hybrid storage split (group A in-memory, group B PostgreSQL)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Postgres everywhere would smother the first lesson behind four EF concepts (change tracker, unit of work, when SaveChanges emits SQL, changed-column UPDATE) and make the naive race harder to reproduce. In-memory everywhere would make the optimistic/pessimistic slices lies \u2014 DbUpdateConcurrencyException never raised, SELECT FOR UPDATE a comment. Accepted cost: two persistence models to hold in your head and non-zero setup.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_inmemoryaccountstore", "label": "InMemoryAccountStore (singleton, deliberately unsafe)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Registered as a singleton because shared mutable process state is the precondition for the race; scoping it would quietly delete the bug. Duplicates the database's Version and a TryWrite compare-and-swap on purpose, to show optimistic concurrency is a pattern rather than an EF feature. Process-local, so it misbehaves under multiple replicas \u2014 which is the point of ADR-0014.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_bankdbcontext", "label": "BankDbContext over PostgreSQL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_ef_inmemory_provider", "label": "EF Core in-memory provider (rejected)", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "Not a shortcut: it implements neither concurrency tokens nor row locking, so tests would pass against a system that is still broken.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_static_dictionary_trap", "label": "static ConcurrentDictionary as source of truth (trap)", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Works perfectly on one instance and corrupts silently on two \u2014 the failure mode this repo demonstrates on purpose. Legitimate in-memory state is caches you can afford to lose, per-request scoped state, and single-writer designs.", "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence", "target": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_hybrid_storage", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_hybrid_storage", "target": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_inmemoryaccountstore", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_hybrid_storage", "target": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_bankdbcontext", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_hybrid_storage", "target": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_ef_inmemory_provider", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_inmemoryaccountstore", "target": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence_static_dictionary_trap", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence", "target": "adr_0014_compose_not_kubernetes", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "adr_0004_hybrid_persistence", "target": "adr_0016_three_tier_test_strategy", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/architecture/adr/0004-hybrid-persistence.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}], "hyperedges": []}